---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { DEFAULT_WEIGHTS, PARTS, historyChanges } from '../lib/lab-standings.mjs';
const { snapshot, archive = false, dates = [], history = [] } = Astro.props;
const changes = historyChanges(snapshot, history);
const rescoredFiles = import.meta.glob('../../data/lab-standings/rescored/*/*.json', {eager:true,import:'default'});
const rescored = (Object.values(rescoredFiles) as any[]).filter(s=>s.date===snapshot.date);
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const labels = ['Capability','Value','Shipping pace','Openness','Developer usage'];
const number = (n: number | null) => n == null ? '—' : n.toFixed(1);
---
<BaseLayout title="Lab Standings — The AI Resource Hub" description="Relative lab standing, with adjustable weights, coverage and source receipts.">
<section class="standings" data-standings={JSON.stringify(snapshot)}>
  <header><p class="eyebrow">The evidence desk · {archive ? 'Frozen archive' : 'Lab Standings'}</p>
  <h1>Who is moving AI forward?</h1><p class="intro">Relative standing, with the evidence left in view. Change the weights to explore what matters to you.</p>
  <p>Snapshot <strong>{snapshot.date}</strong> · Method {snapshot.method} · <a href={`${base}transparency/#lab-standings`}>Sources and calculations</a> · <a href={`${base}labs/`}>Lab directory</a></p></header>
  {snapshot.correction ? <aside class="note"><strong>Corrected scores.</strong> {snapshot.correction.note} <a href={`${base}labs/standings/${snapshot.date}/`}>Original snapshot · as published</a></aside> : snapshot.date === '2026-11-14' && <aside class="note" role="status">Value scores are under correction: the published cohort omitted eligible Epoch labs. <a href={`${base}labs/standings/`}>View corrected standings</a></aside>}
  <aside class="note">Scores measure relative standing: another lab can move your score even when your own inputs stay the same. Missing parts are excluded and weights re-scale; this can help or hurt a lab. Sensitivity ranges are not statistical confidence.</aside>
  {!archive && <fieldset><legend>Your weights <span id="weight-state">Default weights</span></legend>
    <div class="weights">{PARTS.map((part:string,i:number)=><label>{labels[i]} <output for={`weight-${part}`}>{DEFAULT_WEIGHTS[i]}</output><input id={`weight-${part}`} data-weight={i} type="range" min="0" max="100" value={DEFAULT_WEIGHTS[i]} /></label>)}</div>
    <button id="reset-weights" type="button">Reset weights</button><p id="weight-message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </fieldset>}
  <h2>Published standings</h2><p>Ranking eligibility uses default weights and verified coverage. Your weights re-rank that same cohort.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Scores, coverage and changes in relative standing</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rank / lab</th><th scope="col">Score</th><th scope="col">Coverage</th>{labels.map(l=><th scope="col">{l}</th>)}<th scope="col">Sensitivity</th><th scope="col">Change</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{snapshot.rows.map((row:any)=><tr data-lab={row.id}><th scope="row"><span data-rank>{row.rank ?? 'Unranked'}</span> · {row.name}</th><td data-score>{row.eligible ? number(row.score) : '—'}</td><td>{row.coverage}/5 parts<br />{row.observedWeight}/100 weight</td>{PARTS.map((part:string)=><td><a href={`#receipt-${row.id}`}>{number(row.parts[part])}</a></td>)}<td>{snapshot.sensitivity.find((s:any)=>s.id===row.id) ? `${snapshot.sensitivity.find((s:any)=>s.id===row.id).best}–${snapshot.sensitivity.find((s:any)=>s.id===row.id).worst}` : '—'}</td><td>7d: {number(changes.momentum.find((m:any)=>m.id===row.id)?.seven ?? null)}<br />28d: {number(changes.momentum.find((m:any)=>m.id===row.id)?.twentyEight ?? null)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Unranked labs do not yet meet the method's coverage threshold. A dash means unavailable, never zero. Change in relative standing needs comparable frozen snapshots; no history is back-filled.</p>
  <h2>What changed</h2>{snapshot.correction && <p>{snapshot.correction.note}</p>}{changes.previous ? <><p>Compared with {changes.previous}.</p><ul>{changes.changes.map((change:string)=><li>{change}</li>)}</ul>{!changes.changes.length && <p>No rank moves, coverage changes or part changes above the reporting threshold.</p>}</> : <p>This is the first frozen snapshot. No earlier comparable snapshot exists.</p>}
  <p>Shipping pace awaits per-lab release-channel coverage checks. Usage awaits a complete licensed OpenRouter dataset; no keys are read by this build.</p>
  <h2>The receipts</h2><p>Capability uses the same-vintage frontier floor ({number(snapshot.floor)} ECI). Value assumes three input tokens for each output token; prices are USD per million tokens. Developer usage, when available, measures observed top-50 contributions to public OpenRouter traffic; provider tokenisers differ.</p>
  {snapshot.floor == null && <p>No admitted model establishes the year-earlier frontier floor, so capability and value are unavailable for every lab.</p>}
  <p>Openness covers only explicitly reviewed families. All ungraded releases are excluded, including closed-weight status that has not been verified. This is incomplete catalogue coverage, not a lab-wide claim of openness. ECI dates below identify the downloaded vintage; the CSV supplies no separate measurement date.</p>
  {snapshot.rows.map((row:any)=><details id={`receipt-${row.id}`}><summary>{row.name} · inputs and missing data</summary>
    <p>Best ECI: {number(row.best)}. Raw value: {number(row.rawValue)}. Shipping: not checked. Business scale and valuation: unavailable, excluded from score.</p>
    <ul>{snapshot.input.models.filter((m:any)=>m.lab===row.id).map((m:any)=><li><strong>{m.name}</strong>: {m.eci} ECI · release {m.released} · input {m.inputPrice ?? 'unavailable'}, output {m.outputPrice ?? 'unavailable'}.
      {' '}<a href={m.receipt.url}>{m.receipt.source}</a>, as of {m.receipt.asOf}, retrieved {m.receipt.retrievedAt}, {m.receipt.licence}. <code>SHA-256 {m.receipt.version}</code>{m.priceSource && <a href={m.priceSource}>Verified price source</a>}</li>)}</ul>
    <ul>{row.releases.map((r:any)=><li>Family {r.family}: {r.openness} openness credit · {r.released} · <a href={r.licenceSource}>Weights evidence</a> · <a href={r.releaseSource}>Release evidence</a></li>)}</ul>
  </details>)}
  <h2>Weekly archive</h2><p>Snapshots are immutable. New snapshots are proposed through the normal PR pipeline, every Monday at 06:00 UTC; publication waits for review.</p>
  {rescored.map(s=><details><summary>Re-scored cohort under method {s.method}</summary><a href={`${base}labs/standings/rescored/${s.method}/${s.date}.json`}>Re-scored JSON</a><ul>{s.rows.map((r:any)=><li>{r.name}: published {number(snapshot.rows.find((old:any)=>old.id===r.id)?.score ?? null)}; re-scored {number(r.score)}</li>)}</ul></details>)}
  <ul>{dates.map((date:string)=><li><a href={`${base}labs/standings/${date}/`}>{date} · as published</a> · <a href={`${base}labs/standings/${date}.json`}>JSON inputs and scores</a></li>)}</ul>
  <p><a href={snapshot.input.bench.pr}>Day-to-Day Bench</a>: {snapshot.input.bench.status}</p>
  <footer>Epoch AI, <a href="https://epoch.ai/eci">Epoch Capabilities Index</a>, accessed {snapshot.date}, CC BY 4.0. Catalogue evidence: AIRH verified model records. Lab Standings is our own analysis and is not endorsed by these sources.</footer>
</section></BaseLayout>
<script>
import { rank, DEFAULT_WEIGHTS } from '../lib/lab-standings.mjs';
const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-standings]');
const snapshot = JSON.parse(root?.dataset.standings ?? '{}');
const sliders = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-weight]')];
function update() {
 const weights = sliders.map(s=>Number(s.value));
 sliders.forEach(s=>{ const out=s.parentElement?.querySelector('output'); if(out) out.textContent=s.value; });
 const custom=weights.some((w,i)=>w!==DEFAULT_WEIGHTS[i]);
 const badge=document.getElementById('weight-state'); if(badge) badge.textContent=custom?'Your weights':'Default weights';
 const message=document.getElementById('weight-message'); if(message) message.textContent=weights.every(w=>w===0)?'Set at least one weight':'';
 const tbody=document.querySelector('tbody');
 for(const row of rank(snapshot.rows,weights)) {
   const tr=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-lab]')].find(t=>t.dataset.lab===row.id); if(!tr) continue;
   tr.querySelector('[data-rank]')!.textContent=row.rank?.toString() ?? 'Unranked';
   tr.querySelector('[data-score]')!.textContent=row.eligible && row.score!=null ? row.score.toFixed(1) : '—'; tbody?.append(tr);
 }
 const url=new URL(location.href); if(custom) url.searchParams.set('weights',weights.join(',')); else url.searchParams.delete('weights'); history.replaceState(null,'',url);
}
if(sliders.length) {
 const raw=new URL(location.href).searchParams.get('weights'); const parsed=raw?.split(',').map(Number);
 if(parsed?.length===5 && parsed.every(w=>Number.isFinite(w)&&w>=0&&w<=100)) sliders.forEach((s,i)=>s.value=String(parsed[i]));
 sliders.forEach(s=>s.addEventListener('input',update));
 document.getElementById('reset-weights')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{sliders.forEach((s,i)=>s.value=String(DEFAULT_WEIGHTS[i]));update();}); update();
}
</script>
<style>
.standings{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem;color:var(--color-text-primary)}header{max-width:850px;margin-bottom:2rem}.eyebrow{color:var(--color-accent);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.75rem}h1{font:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4.5rem)/1.1 var(--font-display);margin:1rem 0}.intro{font-size:1.25rem;max-width:650px}h2{font:2rem var(--font-display);margin:2rem 0 1rem}p,li{line-height:1.7;margin:.6rem 0}a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;color:var(--color-accent)}.note,fieldset,details{border:1px solid var(--color-border-strong);padding:1.25rem;margin:1rem 0;background:var(--color-bg-card);border-radius:8px}.note{border-left:4px solid var(--color-accent)}.weights{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:1.5rem}label{display:block}input{display:block;width:100%;accent-color:var(--color-accent)}output{float:right}button{border:1px solid;padding:.4rem .8rem;margin-top:1rem;border-radius:4px}.table-wrap{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}th,td{padding:1rem .6rem;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-border-strong)}thead{background:var(--color-bg-tertiary)}caption{text-align:left;padding:.7rem 0}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;display:block;font-size:.7rem}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--color-border-strong);margin-top:2rem;padding-top:1rem;font-size:.85rem}
</style>
